# Artifacts of running build/npm commands from the repository root instead of
# through the Makefile. Ignoring them is a stopgap, not a fix: it only stops them
# showing up in `git status`, and the next bare build recreates them.
#
# /geth is what a bare `go build ./cmd/geth` leaves behind (a ~137 MB unstripped
# binary); `make geth` writes build/bin/geth, which is ignored further up. The
# leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `geth` pattern also matches the cmd/geth
# directory and would ignore the whole cmd/ tree.
#
# /package-lock.json is what npm leaves behind when run in a directory with no
# package.json: it exits ENOENT but still writes an empty lockfile.
/geth
/package-lock.json
